# Finish-up: PR-first publish + SSH-only git

**Branch:** `phase-1-finish-up-pr-ssh`  
**Why:** T0123 finish-up hit (1) blocked direct `main` push (required CI) and (2) skill wording that implied HTTPS-then-SSH fallback.

## Changes

Update finish-up docs so agents:

1. **Never** push `main` directly. Publish via feature-branch PR → wait for required checks → merge on GitHub → pull `main` locally.
2. **Always** use SSH (`git@github.com:blackrook-io/taskmesh.git`) for pull/push — never try HTTPS first.
3. Prefer `gh` for PRs; if missing, GitHub API + `~/.config/taskmesh/github.env`.
4. Archive the plan on the feature branch (in the finish-up commit set) before opening the PR so archive lands with the merge.

